      <section class="ax-panel panel"><h2>Patches to the live release</h2><p class="dim">ARVEX uses file-level delta patches: a launcher downloads only the files whose SHA-256 differs from what it has installed. These are computed from the releases themselves, so a patch can never be applied to the wrong base.</p>${table([{ h: 'Base', v: p => `${esc(p.base.version)} <span class="mono dim">${esc(p.base.id)}</span>` }, { h: 'Target', v: p => `${esc(p.target.version)} <span class="mono dim">${esc(p.target.id)}</span>` }, { h: 'Changed files', v: p => p.files }, { h: 'Removed', v: p => p.removed }, { h: 'Patch size', v: p => `<b>${fmtB(p.size)}</b>` }, { h: 'Full download', v: p => fmtB(p.fullSize) }, { h: 'Hash', v: p => `<span class="mono">${esc(p.hash.slice(0, 12))}…</span>` }], d.patches, { empty: ['No patches yet', 'A patch appears as soon as there is an older release next to the live one.'] })}</section>
